# This file gives a list of source tree locations for each header file
# built as part of the Paragon OS build of /usr/include.  Each directory
# under usr/include is on a line surrounded by brackets: 
#	[ /usr/include/arpa ] 
# and for each file installed into that directory, its location in
# the source cvs repository is given:
#	cmds_libs/src/usr/include/arpa/nameser.h
# A few files are created during the build process (usually by mig)
# and therefore don't really exist in the source tree.  There are also
# a few files installed during the kernel or server builds through symbolic 
# links which are not known to the process which builds usr/include.  
# For files in these two categories, the path to the earliest determinable 
# location of that file in the entire OS build process is printed.
# These paths begin with 'Kernel' or 'Server'.
#
# The presence here of a file does NOT mean that that header file is
# actually installed in /usr/include on a Paragon system.  That is 
# controlled by the ILIST variable in Makefiles.
#
# This file was generated by the 'locate_headers' script.
#
